# Provenance

This repository packages a trained image-to-image model as a container for
grand-challenge.org. It is a derived work; the licence in `LICENSE` (BSD
2-Clause) is the one carried by the upstream project listed below.

## Upstream

`app/models/`, `app/data/`, `app/util/`, `app/options/` and most of
`app/predict.py` come from **pytorch-CycleGAN-and-pix2pix**

- https://github.com/junyanz/pytorch-CycleGAN-and-pix2pix
- Copyright (c) 2017, Phillip Isola and Jun-Yan Zhu
- BSD 2-Clause, reproduced verbatim in `LICENSE`

`app/models/sfm.py` implements the saliency-based feature modulation described
in *Spatial Frequency Modulation for Semantic Segmentation* (Linwei Chen et al.).

## Local additions

- `app/gc_entrypoint.py` — grand-challenge.org entrypoint: reads one
  transmitted-light OME-TIFF and writes four fluorescence OME-TIFFs.
- `app/data/lmc_dataset.py` — index-driven LightMyCells dataset used for
  training; only its `normalise()` helper is reused by the entrypoint.
- `app/predict.py` — tiled inference with a Hann window and the evaluation
  metrics used during development.
- `fetch_weights.py`, `Dockerfile*`, `test/`.

## Model weights

The checkpoints on the `v1` release are derivatives of the LightMyCells
dataset and are published for research use only. They are not part of the
source distribution and are therefore not covered by `LICENSE`.
